<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4760" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλφεσίβοιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bringing in oxen,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθένοι ἀ.</span> maidens <i>who yield
				their parents many oxen as presents from their suitors,</i>
			i.e. <i>much-courted,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.593
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ven.</u>
				119
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ ἀ.,</span> of the Nile,
			water <i>that yields fat oxen</i> (by enriching pastures), <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				855
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πειρήνης ἀ. ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.Aet.
					3.8
				</span></i>
			: pr. n. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀλφεσίβοια</span></b> 
			used at beginning of trim., <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				880
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
